  poem on a single sheet headed "Mineral County High School Circa 1930's" and
  signed it "j jackson 1991." It was found among his papers and does not
  appear in any of his six books or in his manuscript "Please Go to Hell."
  Its subject is Charles S. Mashburn, named as High School Principal in
  John's own high school yearbook. The sheet carries no title of its own;
  the title above is editorial, quoting the poem's first line.
